        },
    },
    .{
        .name = "api begin-upload",
        .Op = v2.BeginUpload,
        .summary = "Begin the upload of one file of a version (one step of 'mopm publish').",
        .usage = "usage: mopm api begin-upload <namespace>/<name> <version> --subdir <linux-64|linux-aarch64|osx-arm64|noarch> --filename <filename> --sha256 <sha256> --size <n> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n",
        .help = "usage: mopm api begin-upload <namespace>/<name> <version> --subdir <linux-64|linux-aarch64|osx-arm64|noarch> --filename <filename> --sha256 <sha256> --size <n> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n\nBegin the upload of one file of a version (one step of 'mopm publish').\n\nPublishing is three steps: begin an upload per file (this call), PUT the\nbytes to the returned URL with the returned headers, then commit\n(`commitPublish`). The registry binds the upload to the caller, the\nname, the version, the sha256 and the size; the presigned URL carries a\nsigned `x-amz-checksum-sha256` and an exact content length so the\nstorage layer itself rejects any other bytes. The URL expires in at\nmost five minutes.\n\nA file over the per-file limit is `payload_too_large` (413). A file\nthat would take the package's live files (published and yanked\nversions; a takedown frees its bytes) over the 10 GB per-project limit\nis `limit_exceeded` (403), which is about the project, not the file:\na smaller file may still fit.\n\narguments:\n  <namespace>/<name>\n      The namespace of the package, a GitHub login in lower case.\n      Normalised package name, the part of the full name after the `/`.\n  <version>\noptions:\n  --subdir <linux-64|linux-aarch64|osx-arm64|noarch>\n      required.\n  --filename <filename>\n      required.\n  --sha256 <sha256>\n      required.\n  --size <n>\n      required. Bytes. At most 100 MB (100,000,000 bytes).\n  --registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>\n      the registry (default prod)\n  --config-dir <dir>\n      where 'mopm login' keeps credentials.json (default ~/.config/mopm)\n  --json\n      print the registry's answer as JSON instead of text\n\nSends POST /api/v2/packages/{namespace}/{name}/{version}/files (beginUpload) with the token 'mopm login' stored, or $MOPM_TOKEN.\n",
        .token = true,
        .body = .flags,
        .args = &.{
            .{ .meta = "<namespace>/<name>", .key = "namespace/name", .full_name = true },
            .{ .meta = "<version>", .key = "version" },
        },
        .flags = &.{
            .{ .flag = "--subdir", .meta = "<linux-64|linux-aarch64|osx-arm64|noarch>", .key = "subdir", .in = .body, .kind = .enumeration, .values = &.{ "linux-64", "linux-aarch64", "osx-arm64", "noarch" }, .required = true },
            .{ .flag = "--filename", .meta = "<filename>", .key = "filename", .in = .body, .kind = .string, .required = true },
            .{ .flag = "--sha256", .meta = "<sha256>", .key = "sha256", .in = .body, .kind = .string, .required = true },
            .{ .flag = "--size", .meta = "<n>", .key = "size", .in = .body, .kind = .integer, .required = true },
        },
    },
    .{
        .name = "api commit-publish",
        .Op = v2.CommitPublish,
        .summary = "Commit the uploads of a version (one step of 'mopm publish').",
        .usage = "usage: mopm api commit-publish <namespace>/<name> <version> --upload-ids <upload_ids>... [--manifest-sha256 <manifest_sha256>] [--source-commit <source_commit>] [--description <description>] [--license <license>] [--repository <repository>] [--homepage <homepage>] [--keywords <keywords>...] [--readme <readme>] [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n",
        .help = "usage: mopm api commit-publish <namespace>/<name> <version> --upload-ids <upload_ids>... [--manifest-sha256 <manifest_sha256>] [--source-commit <source_commit>] [--description <description>] [--license <license>] [--repository <repository>] [--homepage <homepage>] [--keywords <keywords>...] [--readme <readme>] [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n\nCommit the uploads of a version (one step of 'mopm publish').\n\nAsynchronous. The registry answers 202 with a status URL; the CLI\npolls it. Each upload id is single use and must belong to the caller\nand to this name and version. Committing the same upload ids again\nwhile the version is still `pending` resumes the same publish. A\nversion that exists in any other state is refused with\n`version_exists`, whose message carries the sha256 already published;\na client that wants \"succeed if these exact bytes are already\npublished\" compares that sha256 with its own (or reads `getVersion`).\nThe file set of a version is fixed at commit.\n\nThe optional display fields (`description`, `license`, `repository`,\n`homepage`, `keywords`, `readme`) are checked here, stored on the\nversion when it is published and served back by `getVersion`. A value\nthat breaks its rule is `invalid_request`. A client that sends none gets\na version without them, as before.\n\nThe optional `source_commit` is the git commit id the version was built\nfrom (40 or 64 lowercase hex digits). It is stored once with the version,\nreturned by `getVersion` as `source_commit`, and left out for a version\ncommitted without one. The registry only checks its form: it is not verified\nagainst the archives or the caller, and versions are never compared or\nordered by it.\n\narguments:\n  <namespace>/<name>\n      The namespace of the package, a GitHub login in lower case.\n      Normalised package name, the part of the full name after the `/`.\n  <version>\noptions:\n  --upload-ids <upload_ids>...\n      required.\n  --manifest-sha256 <manifest_sha256>\n      Optional. The SHA-256 of the bytes of `lib/mojo/<import name>.mopm.json` in the archives (what `mopm pack` prints). When given\n      it is checked: a value that is not 64 lowercase hex digits is `invalid_request`, and an archive whose manifest hashes\n      to something else is rejected `sha256_mismatch`. When absent, nothing is checked and the version holds the hash the\n      registry computes from the archives; then every file of the version must carry the same manifest bytes, or the publish is\n      rejected `manifest_invalid`. When given, a file whose manifest hashes to something else is `sha256_mismatch`, so at\n      most the files that carry the given manifest bytes pass.\n  --source-commit <source_commit>\n      Optional. The git commit the version was built from (see `SourceCommit`). Stored once with the version and served by\n      `getVersion`; the registry does not verify it. Committing the same upload ids again must repeat it (or its absence): a\n      repeat that states another value is refused `version_exists`, and the stored value does not change.\n  --description <description>\n      `[package] description` of this version's mopm.toml: one line, no line breaks. Stored on the version and served back by `getVersion`.\n  --license <license>\n      `[package] license`, an SPDX expression.\n  --repository <repository>\n      An https URL.\n  --homepage <homepage>\n      An https URL.\n  --keywords <keywords>...\n  --readme <readme>\n      Untrusted Markdown, stored verbatim: the registry does not sanitize it, so a consumer must sanitize it,\n      disable raw HTML and treat links as untrusted. Same for `description` and `license` (plain text).\n      At most 64 KiB: 65,536 bytes of UTF-8 (the registry counts\n      bytes, not characters, so non-ASCII text uses more of it). This is\n      the cap the read API serves, so a larger readme is refused with\n      `invalid_request` rather than stored and never shown. `maxLength`\n      below is in characters and can only bound the byte count from\n      above.\n  --registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>\n      the registry (default prod)\n  --config-dir <dir>\n      where 'mopm login' keeps credentials.json (default ~/.config/mopm)\n  --json\n      print the registry's answer as JSON instead of text\n\nSends POST /api/v2/packages/{namespace}/{name}/{version}/publish (commitPublish) with the token 'mopm login' stored, or $MOPM_TOKEN.\n",
        .token = true,
        .body = .flags,
        .args = &.{
            .{ .meta = "<namespace>/<name>", .key = "namespace/name", .full_name = true },
            .{ .meta = "<version>", .key = "version" },
        },
        .flags = &.{
            .{ .flag = "--upload-ids", .meta = "<upload_ids>...", .key = "upload_ids", .in = .body, .kind = .string, .required = true, .repeated = true },
            .{ .flag = "--manifest-sha256", .meta = "<manifest_sha256>", .key = "manifest_sha256", .in = .body, .kind = .string },
            .{ .flag = "--source-commit", .meta = "<source_commit>", .key = "source_commit", .in = .body, .kind = .string },
            .{ .flag = "--description", .meta = "<description>", .key = "description", .in = .body, .kind = .string },
            .{ .flag = "--license", .meta = "<license>", .key = "license", .in = .body, .kind = .string },
            .{ .flag = "--repository", .meta = "<repository>", .key = "repository", .in = .body, .kind = .string },
            .{ .flag = "--homepage", .meta = "<homepage>", .key = "homepage", .in = .body, .kind = .string },
            .{ .flag = "--keywords", .meta = "<keywords>...", .key = "keywords", .in = .body, .kind = .string, .repeated = true },
            .{ .flag = "--readme", .meta = "<readme>", .key = "readme", .in = .body, .kind = .string },
        },
    },
    .{
        .name = "publish status",
        .Op = v2.GetPublishStatus,
        .summary = "Show how a publish is going.",
        .usage = "usage: mopm publish status <publish_id> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n",
        .help = "usage: mopm publish status <publish_id> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n\nShow how a publish is going.\n\n`pending`, `validating` and `indexing` are in progress; `published` and\n`rejected` are final. A rejected publish burns the version number.\nA publish that passed can still carry `warnings`.\n\narguments:\n  <publish_id>\noptions:\n  --registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>\n      the registry (default prod)\n  --config-dir <dir>\n      where 'mopm login' keeps credentials.json (default ~/.config/mopm)\n  --json\n      print the registry's answer as JSON instead of text\n\nSends GET /api/v2/publishes/{publish_id} (getPublishStatus) with the token 'mopm login' stored, or $MOPM_TOKEN.\n",
        .token = true,
        .body = .none,
        .args = &.{
            .{ .meta = "<publish_id>", .key = "publish_id" },
        },
    },
    .{
        .name = "api create-group",
        .Op = v2.CreateGroup,
        .summary = "Create or continue a publish group (one step of 'mopm publish --staged').",
        .usage = "usage: mopm api create-group --body <file> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n",
        .help = "usage: mopm api create-group --body <file> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n\nCreate or continue a publish group (one step of 'mopm publish --staged').\n\nA group is a set of versions, at most one per package, that are meant to be published together. This call\ndeclares the whole set up front (each member's name, version and files with their sha256 and size) and\nreserves the version numbers; the caller then PUTs each file to the URL it is given. Creating a group\npublishes nothing and makes nothing visible.\n\nThe token must be an API token with the `publish` or `stage` scope for every member's package, and the caller must be\nable to write the namespace of each package; or a CI identity token minted by `exchangeOidcToken` for a publisher of the\nnamespace, which must name every member's package and version. The first member\nthat fails any of these refuses the whole group and is named in the error. A number that a published version\nalready holds is `version_exists`; one that another group is still using is `group_conflict`. A\n`group_conflict` carries a `reason` (see `Error`) that tells the causes apart without reading the message.\n\nThe id of a group is a function of the caller and the declared set: the same request again is the same group. The\nderivation is a stable interface, so a client can compute the id itself and read the group with `getGroup` (a 404\n`group_not_found` means there is no such group of the caller's). The id is `grp_` followed by the first 32 lowercase hex\ndigits of the SHA-256 of the UTF-8 bytes of the compact JSON text (no white space) of the array\n`[actor, set]`. `actor` is `u:<GitHub account id>` for an account's token, including a CI token that acts for an\naccount, and `ci:gh-repo:<repository id>` for a configured CI publisher's own token. `set` is the array of members\nsorted by full name, each member `[name, version, files]`, with `files` the array of the member's files sorted by\nthe text `<subdir>/<filename>`, each file `[subdir, filename, sha256, size]` (`size` a JSON integer). The order of\nmembers and files in the request, `on_overlap`, a member's `readme` and every other option are not part of it. For the actor `u:1234` and\nthe one file `linux-64/mojo-komira-ai.alpha-1.0.0-mojo1.0.0_0.conda` (sha256 `a` repeated 64 times, size 1000) of\n`komira-ai/alpha` 1.0.0, the text hashed is\n`[\"u:1234\",[[\"komira-ai/alpha\",\"1.0.0\",[[\"linux-64\",\"mojo-komira-ai.alpha-1.0.0-mojo1.0.0_0.conda\",\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",1000]]]]]`\nand the id is `grp_598a7e4a7e56109c58051a434f3be338`. More vectors are in the registry's test fixtures. A change to the\nderivation would be a new id prefix, never a different hash under `grp_`. The hosted registry derives ids this way; the\nfake registry's ids are opaque and a client must not compute them.\n\nRepeating the request while the group is `open` returns `200` and continues it (a reply with `reserving` has not\nreached every member yet; send the same request again), with fresh upload URLs for the files not yet in\nstorage. Repeating it for a group that ended without committing (`expired`, `aborted`, `rejected`,\n`superseded`) opens it again with the next `attempt` (`201`). A group that is `validating`, `committed` or\n`visible` is returned as it is. A `failed` group has burned its numbers: `group_conflict`.\n\nA caller has a limited number of open groups. A different set that shares a version with one of the caller's\nown open groups supersedes it; a group that is validating is never superseded. With `on_overlap: refuse` it is\nrefused instead (`group_conflict`, reason `overlap_refused`) and nothing is ended. The groups a create ended are\nlisted in `superseded` of its answer. A group that is past its\n`deadline_at` is expired by the next request that meets it. A group costs its number of files from a daily\nallowance of its own, once per attempt, which is not the allowance of single publishes.\n\nA registry that lists `group_readme_objects` in the `features` of `getHealth` also takes a `readme` on a member: the\nSHA-256 and size of the member's readme. It answers, for such a member, where to PUT the readme (`readme` of the\nmember's answer, see `GroupUploadReadme`), and `commitGroup` then names the readme by that digest and size instead of\ncarrying its text. A `readme` that is not `{sha256, size}` of a readme of 1 to 65536 bytes is `invalid_request`, and\nthe message names the member. A registry that does not list the feature ignores the field and answers none.\n\nGroup publishing is off unless the registry has enabled it for the caller. Until then this call is answered\n`route_not_found`; reading and aborting a group that exists keep working.\n\noptions:\n  --body <file>\n      the request body, JSON (`-`: standard input), as `CreateGroupRequest` of spec/api/openapi-v2.yaml\n  --registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>\n      the registry (default prod)\n  --config-dir <dir>\n      where 'mopm login' keeps credentials.json (default ~/.config/mopm)\n  --json\n      print the registry's answer as JSON instead of text\n\nSends POST /api/v2/groups (createGroup) with the token 'mopm login' stored, or $MOPM_TOKEN.\n",
        .token = true,
        .body = .file,
    },
    .{
        .name = "group status",
        .Op = v2.GetGroup,
        .summary = "Show a publish group: its state, its members and its yank.",
        .usage = "usage: mopm group status <group_id> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n",
        .help = "usage: mopm group status <group_id> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n\nShow a publish group: its state, its members and its yank.\n\nThe group's status, attempt and deadline, and the state of each member: `pending` (its number is not reserved\nyet), `reserved`, `staged`, `published` or `yanked`. Each member also lists its `files`: the facts the caller declared at\n`createGroup`, and, while the group is `open`, whether each file is in storage. The read reserves and charges nothing (it only\nexpires a group past its deadline), so it is the way to see a group, whatever its status, without `createGroup` (which reopens a group that ended).\nNeeds a token with `stage` or `publish`. Readable by the caller who created the group and by an account that can write the namespace of every\npackage in it; anyone else gets `group_not_found`. A group past its deadline that was still open is expired\nby this read.\n\narguments:\n  <group_id>\noptions:\n  --registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>\n      the registry (default prod)\n  --config-dir <dir>\n      where 'mopm login' keeps credentials.json (default ~/.config/mopm)\n  --json\n      print the registry's answer as JSON instead of text\n\nSends GET /api/v2/groups/{group_id} (getGroup) with the token 'mopm login' stored, or $MOPM_TOKEN.\n",
        .token = true,
        .body = .none,
        .args = &.{
            .{ .meta = "<group_id>", .key = "group_id" },
        },
    },
    .{
        .name = "group abort",
        .Op = v2.AbortGroup,
        .summary = "End an open publish group without publishing it.",
        .usage = "usage: mopm group abort <group_id> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n",
        .help = "usage: mopm group abort <group_id> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n\nEnd an open publish group without publishing it.\n\nEnds a group that is `open`. Its reserved version numbers are free again: another group, or a single publish,\nmay take them. Repeating the call on an aborted group is a no-op and returns 200. A group in any other state\n(`validating`, `committed`, `expired`, ...) is `group_not_open`. Allowed for the same callers as `getGroup`: a token with `stage` or `publish`.\n\narguments:\n  <group_id>\noptions:\n  --registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>\n      the registry (default prod)\n  --config-dir <dir>\n      where 'mopm login' keeps credentials.json (default ~/.config/mopm)\n  --json\n      print the registry's answer as JSON instead of text\n\nSends DELETE /api/v2/groups/{group_id} (abortGroup) with the token 'mopm login' stored, or $MOPM_TOKEN.\n",
        .token = true,
        .body = .none,
        .args = &.{
            .{ .meta = "<group_id>", .key = "group_id" },
        },
    },
    .{
        .name = "api commit-group",
        .Op = v2.CommitGroup,
        .summary = "Commit a publish group (one step of 'mopm publish --staged').",
        .usage = "usage: mopm api commit-group <group_id> --body <file> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n",
        .help = "usage: mopm api commit-group <group_id> --body <file> [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n\nCommit a publish group (one step of 'mopm publish --staged').\n\nAsynchronous. The caller has created the group and PUT every file to the URL it was given; this call hands over what\nthe archives cannot say for themselves, one entry per member: the optional `manifest_sha256` of its embedded manifest (checked when given, as in\n`commitPublish`), the optional display fields (the same rules as `commitPublish`) and the optional `source_commit` (the\nsame rules, informational and unverified; it lands on that member's version only). Every member of the group is listed exactly once.\n\nThe registry checks that the group is `open`, not past its `deadline_at`, that every member is reserved and that every\nfile is in storage at its declared size, stores the request, moves the group to `validating` and answers 202. It then\nvalidates every member's archives; if every one is valid it copies the files into the channel and commits the group:\nthe members become visible together to the read API, as `published` at the commit time. A member whose archive is not\nvalid, a deadline that passes, or an upload more than 18 hours old ends the group `rejected` before anything is copied\n(its version numbers are free again); a failure after the copies began ends it `failed`, and its version numbers are\nburned. Read `getGroup` for where it is: `status` and, for a group that ended, `failure`.\n\nThe same request again resumes: while the group is `validating` it queues the validation again (one job), and for a\ngroup that has committed it answers `200` as it is. A different request for a group that already has one is refused.\nA group that is not open (`aborted`, `expired`, `rejected`, ...) is refused with `group_commit_refused`; create it\nagain with the same request to open it again. A commit is a write: read-only mode refuses it. It is not gated by the\nswitch that enables group creation, since a group that exists is finished whatever the switch says.\n\nThe token must have the `publish` scope (or, for a CI identity token, be the `publish` token of the exchange). A token with\nonly `stage` is refused as `scope_missing`, and the group stays as it was.\n\nA member's `readme` is either the text (a string) or, at a registry that lists `group_readme_objects` in the\n`features` of `getHealth`, the `{sha256, size}` of a readme the caller has PUT to the URL `createGroup` gave. With\ntext, the request is one body that holds the display fields of every member (a readme is up to 64 KiB), so a group\nof many members with readmes can exceed what the gateway accepts. With the object form the body holds a digest and a\nsize for each readme (under 100 bytes), so its size does not depend on the readmes and a group of up to 500\nmembers stays far below any limit of the gateway.\n\narguments:\n  <group_id>\noptions:\n  --body <file>\n      the request body, JSON (`-`: standard input), as `CommitGroupRequest` of spec/api/openapi-v2.yaml\n  --registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>\n      the registry (default prod)\n  --config-dir <dir>\n      where 'mopm login' keeps credentials.json (default ~/.config/mopm)\n  --json\n      print the registry's answer as JSON instead of text\n\nSends POST /api/v2/groups/{group_id}/commit (commitGroup) with the token 'mopm login' stored, or $MOPM_TOKEN.\n",
        .token = true,
        .body = .file,
        .args = &.{
            .{ .meta = "<group_id>", .key = "group_id" },
        },
    },
    .{
        .name = "group yank",
        .Op = v2.YankGroup,
        .summary = "Yank every version a publish group published.",
        .usage = "usage: mopm group yank <group_id> [--reason <reason>] [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n",
        .help = "usage: mopm group yank <group_id> [--reason <reason>] [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n\nYank every version a publish group published.\n\nThe body is that of `setYanked`. `yanked: true` yanks the group's versions that are `published`; `yanked: false` restores\nexactly the versions that yank changed. Allowed for an account that can write the namespace of every package in it now, whether or not it created the\ngroup (a token outlives a membership change; an account that has lost the right is refused with `not_namespace_member`), with a token\nthat has the `yank` or `publish` scope for every member (read-only mode refuses it).\n\nOnly a group that is `visible` can be yanked or unyanked; a group that has not committed, or whose files are still being\nreleased after the commit, is refused with `group_not_settled`, as is a yank while an unyank of the group is running and the\nother way round. Asynchronous: the request records the intent, answers 202 and returns the group; the versions are yanked\n(or restored) by a job, then repodata and the sparse index follow, and the group's `yank.state` reaches `yanked` (or\n`restored`) when they are written. A version somebody yanked by hand before the group's yank stays yanked, and is not\nrestored by the group's unyank. The same request again while the yank or unyank runs answers 202 as it is; a group already as\nasked (yanked and `yanked: true`, or never yanked or restored and `yanked: false`) answers 200 as it is.\n\narguments:\n  <group_id>\noptions:\n  --reason <reason>\n      Required when `yanked` is true. Shown to people who locked the version.\n  --registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>\n      the registry (default prod)\n  --config-dir <dir>\n      where 'mopm login' keeps credentials.json (default ~/.config/mopm)\n  --json\n      print the registry's answer as JSON instead of text\n\nSends PUT /api/v2/groups/{group_id}/yank (yankGroup) with the token 'mopm login' stored, or $MOPM_TOKEN.\n",
