        .help = "usage: mopm yank <namespace>/<name> <version> [--reason <reason>] [--registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>] [--config-dir <dir>] [--json]\n\nYank a version: new resolutions no longer pick it.\n\n`yanked: true` hides the version from new resolution; its files stay\ndownloadable at their exact URLs, so existing locks keep working.\n`yanked: false` restores it. Allowed for an account that can write the\nnamespace, or a token with the `yank` or `publish` scope for the package. Repeating the same change\nis a no-op and returns 200. A change the version's state does not\nallow is refused with `invalid_transition` (409): yanking a version\nthat is still pending or is tombstoned, unyanking a version that is\nnot yanked, or any change to a tombstoned version. A tombstoned\nversion (taken down by an administrator) never changes state.\n\narguments:\n  <namespace>/<name>\n      The namespace of the package, a GitHub login in lower case.\n      Normalised package name, the part of the full name after the `/`.\n  <version>\noptions:\n  --reason <reason>\n      Required when `yanked` is true. Shown to people who locked the version.\n  --registry <prod|gamma|beta|url>\n      the registry (default prod)\n  --config-dir <dir>\n      where 'mopm login' keeps credentials.json (default ~/.config/mopm)\n  --json\n      print the registry's answer as JSON instead of text\n\nSends PUT /api/v2/packages/{namespace}/{name}/{version}/yank (setYanked) with the token 'mopm login' stored, or $MOPM_TOKEN.\n",
